KNOWNBUG libcxx20
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++
^VERIFICATION
^EXIT=(0|10)$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
Template argument deduction for endl(cerr) fails on libc++-20.
Root cause: basic_ostream<char,...> loses ID_C_template metadata
when typecheck_compound_type swaps the incomplete type with the
complete type (line 211). The full_template_args set by
class_template_symbol are also lost. Without this metadata,
guess_template_args can't match the struct against the template
pattern to deduce _CharT and _Traits.
Fix: preserve full_template_args during the type swap in
typecheck_compound_type. This was verified to work but also
requires not preserving template_class_instance (which causes
invariant violations in other tests).
